Krita Nova 58 - Android: tapping a number field in a QML panel opens the keyboard

On Android, tapping the Text tool's font size (and the other slider number
fields of the QML panels - the Text Properties docker, the text tool
options) only moved the slider to the tapped spot; a long press opened the
field for typing but no keyboard came up, so the size could not be typed.

- On Android a tap (no drag) opens the field for typing; dragging still
  changes the value. Desktop behaviour is unchanged.
- When the field opens for typing on Android, the keyboard is asked for
  (the text input got its focus from code, which Android does not answer
  by itself); it closes again when editing finishes or is cancelled.
- The QML host widget takes the focus on a tap and accepts keyboard input
  on Android.

